WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.000
Can you successfully follow up one of the most&nbsp;
beloved comic book movies of all time? Is it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.020
possible to make a dude with teeny wings on&nbsp;
his feet and little green shorts look cool?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:15.600
The answer is that yes, you can — but not&nbsp;
without a few compromises along the way.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.160
Warning: Major spoilers for Black&nbsp;
Panther: Wakanda Forever ahead.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.380
Costume designer Ruth E. Carter — who&nbsp;
became the first Black woman ever to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.160
win the Oscar in the category for her&nbsp;
work on the first "Black Panther" — has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:33.960
really outdone herself this time with her&nbsp;
return in "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever."

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:39.720
The costumes in "Wakanda Forever" range from&nbsp;
college kid streetwear to high-tech diving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:46.200
suits to ceremonial funeral garb and so much&nbsp;
more. Queen Ramonda's many royal ensembles are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:53.040
standouts. In various shades of jewel tones, from&nbsp;
form-fitting to billowing, her gowns all still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.800
share the same design motif thanks to similar&nbsp;
prints and coordinating jewelry. Nakia's bright&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:04.620
and casual clothes from her scenes as a Haitian&nbsp;
teacher suit the character's personality just as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:10.500
much as her vibrant greenish War Dog armor. And&nbsp;
the incredible quality of Namor's movie-specific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.780
design does much of the work of transforming&nbsp;
the character from a longtime comics oddball&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:21.120
into a mythical anti-hero god. The outfits&nbsp;
are all visually interesting yet believable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.280
and how they pull inspiration from real&nbsp;
culture — ancient and modern — is commendable.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.306
"She really can make you, like, click&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.306 --> 00:01:32.468
into place with the costumes she puts&nbsp;
you in. She's a storyteller first."

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:38.280
Usually, if the camera is going to linger&nbsp;
on a particular shot in an MCU film, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:44.520
because of fight choreography or expensive CGI. In&nbsp;
"Wakanda Forever," the camera frequently lingers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:49.740
on characters just looking awesome in their&nbsp;
clothes; Carter's creations are that breathtaking.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.880
While none of the designs in&nbsp;
"Wakanda Forever" are misses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:59.100
the fleet of vehicles in the film is probably&nbsp;
the weakest element, conceptually. On their own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:03.660
all the modes of transportation range&nbsp;
from fine to pretty cool. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:10.140
the aircraft that arrives to transport T'Challa's&nbsp;
vibranium coffin almost resembles the face of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:14.460
black panther when it's lit up and viewed from&nbsp;
below, which is an interesting visual touch.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:19.860
But when it actually levitates the casket&nbsp;
up in its tractor beam during the funeral,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:25.860
it completely takes viewers out of what's an&nbsp;
otherwise serious, somber moment. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.780
some of the other planes that are deployed to&nbsp;
evacuate citizens during the flooding of Wakanda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:36.600
look vaguely and curiously like simpler versions&nbsp;
of Nova Corps starships from "The Guardians of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:41.580
the Galaxy." Even the large Wakandan ship&nbsp;
that serves as the main battleground for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:46.740
the film's final fight feels kind of boring&nbsp;
and unmemorable. "Wakanda Forever's" vehicles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:52.320
feel Marvel-y...they're just not the sleekest&nbsp;
or most exciting that the MCU has to offer.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:58.920
"Wakanda Forever'' confronts heavy and pressing&nbsp;
global issues head-on. The film can be read as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:04.080
metaphor for nuclear proliferation. The Wakandans&nbsp;
possess the world's most powerful resource,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:10.080
and everyone else is in a race to catch up. In&nbsp;
the past, real civilizations like Nazi Germany&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:15.780
or the Soviet Union have been the antagonists&nbsp;
in Marvel films. This time, it's modern America,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:22.020
France, and the rest of the United Nations. Being&nbsp;
outgunned by a small African country has exposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:29.220
the west's hypocrisy. New CIA director Valentina&nbsp;
Allegra de Fontaine openly admits she dreams about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:34.980
the U.S. controlling Earth's vibranium supply, but&nbsp;
a large chunk of the international intelligence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.900
community is willing to resort to some pretty&nbsp;
villainous tactics to get that sweet magic metal.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:45.900
At a United Nations meeting, Queen Ramonda&nbsp;
dramatically announces that Wakanda has foiled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:50.880
a plot to steal vibranium from one of their&nbsp;
secret research facilities by having the Dora&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:56.100
Milaje march the captive offenders before&nbsp;
their heads of state. She argues it's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:01.260
vibranium's power she fears, but what humans&nbsp;
would do with it. It's a bold move to call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:06.000
out these nations this way, but it works with&nbsp;
the story "Wakanda Forever" is trying to tell.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:12.480
The sequel is also interested in colonialism and&nbsp;
its effects on indigenous people. In a flashback,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:18.180
we see that Spanish conquistadors brought&nbsp;
ruin to Namor's people. His anger at and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:22.860
distrust of the surface world stems from&nbsp;
the fallout. Even the film's resolution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:27.780
in which two superpowered beings agree to&nbsp;
put vengeance aside and de-escalate their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:33.420
fight plays into the nuclear symbolism and the&nbsp;
real world, Cold War policy of Mutually Assured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:39.120
Destruction. "Wakanda Forever's" politics aren't&nbsp;
left or right; they're clear-eyed and practical.

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:46.560
Dominique Thorne is a likable addition to&nbsp;
the MCU as Riri Williams, aka Ironheart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:51.840
but the plot that introduces her isn't as good&nbsp;
as the character herself or Thorne's performance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:57.180
It's entertaining and gives "Wakanda Forever" some&nbsp;
propulsion early on, but it's also underbaked.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.260
"That can't be good."

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:05.040
Riri's vibranium detecting school project ends&nbsp;
up in the hands of covert US operatives who are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:09.330
using it to find heretofore unknown&nbsp;
quantities of vibranium from a sea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:14.100
bed in the Atlantic Ocean. This interference&nbsp;
threatens Namor and his people's way of life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:19.260
and kicks off the conflict between&nbsp;
Namor and Wakanda. Namor wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:24.180
kill the scientist who made the machine,&nbsp;
while Shuri is determined to protect Riri.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:30.180
Unfortunately, Riri's actual involvement in&nbsp;
the story doesn't amount to much. There's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:35.340
fun moment early on where she helps Shuri and&nbsp;
Okoye escape the local police with the help of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:40.800
her homemade Ironheart suit, but after that she's&nbsp;
little more than a plot football. Hardly anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:45.660
she does from this point forward affects the&nbsp;
events of the film. Her more polished Ironheart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:50.400
armor helps Shuri's plan to trap Namor in the&nbsp;
final battle, but her character's motivations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:55.140
aren't much more than "don't die, help Wakanda."&nbsp;
The movie keeps trying to tell us that she'll be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:59.820
important with a few hints of her backstory,&nbsp;
but we rarely see that importance take shape.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:05.700
Like America Chavez in "Doctor Strange and the&nbsp;
Multiverse of Madness," Riri is an exciting new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:09.900
character with tons of potential who's&nbsp;
reduced mostly to a human MacGuffin.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:15.840
One of the smartest decisions Ryan Coogler&nbsp;
and company made was swapping Marvel Comics'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:21.780
Atlantis for the mythical Mesoamerican city&nbsp;
of Talokan — a fictionalization of Tlālōcān,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:27.000
one of the Aztec afterlives. Of course, the&nbsp;
decision was more or less made for them since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:31.920
Warner Bros. beat Marvel to the screen with&nbsp;
Aquaman. Nevermind that Namor came first in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:36.960
the comics — Aquaman has always been the&nbsp;
better known half-blood king of Atlantis.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:40.560
"Wakanda Forever" changed&nbsp;
that bit of Namor's backstory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:45.360
and it works wonderfully. In the film version,&nbsp;
his origin story has everything to do with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:51.120
vibranium meteorite and Spanish conquistadors.&nbsp;
Rooting Namor in Aztec and Mayan history and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:55.080
culture is a vast improvement on an&nbsp;
already intriguing comics character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:58.860
and the Talokan that the filmmakers&nbsp;
created for him rivals Wakanda.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:04.260
Born with prolonged life and the ability&nbsp;
to breathe air and water, as well as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:10.140
gift of flight because of the wings on his&nbsp;
feet, Namor is given the title K'uk'ulkan or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:15.780
Feathered Serpent God, a supernatural entity&nbsp;
pulled from Mesoamerican religion. As a boy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:20.640
he becomes a legend to his people when he&nbsp;
uses his power to fight back against Spanish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:26.580
colonizers. Since the MCU has been interested in&nbsp;
geopolitical issues and gods lately, this updated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:32.220
version of Namor and his home of Talokan fits&nbsp;
right into the cinematic universe's trajectory.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:38.580
Okoye became one of the breakout characters in&nbsp;
"Black Panther" for good reason. The leader of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:45.600
the Dora Milaje was as stoic and tough as anyone&nbsp;
in the first film, save for T'Challa himself. Her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:50.220
storyline saw her wrestle with the question of&nbsp;
what to do when Killmonger assumed the throne.

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:55.800
Though Danai Gurira is every bit as captivating&nbsp;
in "Wakanda Forever," the film doesn't do her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:01.140
justice. She gets a stunning entrance when the&nbsp;
Dora Milaje infiltrate the French operatives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:06.300
planning to steal and study vibranium, but for&nbsp;
much of the second half of the movie, she's MIA.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:13.080
When Shuri and Riri are captured, Ramonda blames&nbsp;
Okoye and dismisses her from duty. Devastated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:18.240
one of the best characters and best actors&nbsp;
in the film is sidelined. In a movie with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:22.560
way too many characters to fully develop,&nbsp;
it's a shame that one of the franchise's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:26.580
best doesn't get enough screen time&nbsp;
to continue her own fascinating story.

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:33.540
In the comics, Namor and Black Panther have&nbsp;
a real love-hate relationship. Sometimes they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:36.660
align themselves and their kingdoms&nbsp;
with each other for a common cause,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:41.880
and they are both superhuman rulers of super&nbsp;
secret societies. But more often than not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:45.540
they're at each other's throats.&nbsp;
With "Wakanda Forever," somebody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:51.000
other than T'Challa had to put on the Black&nbsp;
Panther's mask — and face off against Namor.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:55.980
Though Chadwick Boseman and Tenoch Huerta&nbsp;
would've been phenomenal scene partners,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.980 --> 00:09:01.860
Huerta and Letitia Wright's Shuri have a totally&nbsp;
different chemistry that takes Namor and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:06.120
Black Panther's love-hate relationship&nbsp;
to another level. In this adaptation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:11.580
there's actually some romantic tension between&nbsp;
the mutant god king and the scientist princess.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:17.700
It's never made explicit except for that pretty&nbsp;
high-value gift of his beloved mother's bracelet.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:23.340
When Namor offers to take Shuri to Talokan and&nbsp;
wistfully confides in her that she's the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:27.660
surface human ever to have seen their&nbsp;
world, it's not hard to imagine them as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:33.000
allies — and maybe something more. There's&nbsp;
a tragic irony to the idea that these two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:38.100
understand each other but are destined to&nbsp;
become enemies, for a time at least. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:43.620
Ramonda orders Nakia to invade his home and&nbsp;
she kills some of his people to rescue Shuri,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:50.280
he retaliates by flooding Wakanda and indirectly&nbsp;
killing many citizens, including Ramonda herself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:55.860
Even their final showdown is charged with&nbsp;
shared emotion; they're both isolated, angry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.860 --> 00:10:01.620
and — as Namor's name means in this take on the&nbsp;
character — without love. But if only broken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:07.020
people can be great leaders, there are big things&nbsp;
ahead for Namor and Shuri, together or not.

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:11.760
"Both nations want the same thing, which&nbsp;
is to preserve and to protect their people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:15.000
but they're willing to go&nbsp;
about it in different ways."

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:19.680
When the MCU first took us to Wakanda,&nbsp;
viewers got to meet a plethora of new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:23.700
characters including more people of color&nbsp;
and more women than the franchise had ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:28.080
seen before. In addition to T'Challa,&nbsp;
his supporting cast of all had unique,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:33.420
fleshed-out personalities of their own. "Wakanda&nbsp;
Forever" advertised that audiences would become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:37.920
acquainted with a second superpowered&nbsp;
civilization. The trailers and casting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:43.260
news indicated that Attuma and Namora — two&nbsp;
important characters from the comics — would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:48.240
be living and fighting alongside Namor, just&nbsp;
as Okoye and M'Baku did in "Black Panther."

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:53.640
In the comics, Attuma is a barbarian-like&nbsp;
Atlantean who believes that he ought to rule&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:57.960
instead of Namor. And throughout her comics&nbsp;
history, Namora has been everything from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:04.080
Namor's implied lover to his cousin to a clone.&nbsp;
Even with the change from Atlantis to Talokan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:09.000
there's enough backstory to have made Attuma&nbsp;
and Namora more unique characters. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:13.800
one of "Wakanda Forever's" weak spots is the&nbsp;
regrettable underdevelopment of its Talokanil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:18.420
supporting cast. They're deployed — much&nbsp;
like "Infinity War's" Ebony Maw and Proxima&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:22.440
Midnight — like a henchman and henchwoman&nbsp;
who are little more than bodies in the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:26.820
until it's time for the main characters&nbsp;
to fight Namor. We get little more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:32.040
a hint that Namora is dissatisfied with Namor&nbsp;
and Shuri's peaceful resolution near the end.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:37.800
It's become a refrain that most Marvel movies&nbsp;
are great…until the final act devolves into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:43.320
a CGI soup, the main ingredients of which&nbsp;
are faceless hordes, Kaiju-like monsters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:48.780
and of course, sky beams and portals. Most of the&nbsp;
criticism of the first "Black Panther," in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:53.700
came for its lackluster last-act digital&nbsp;
effects. It seems the filmmakers have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:57.720
learned from their mistakes and&nbsp;
from worn-out MCU tropes. The final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.720 --> 00:12:02.760
battle in "Wakanda Forever" is one of Marvel&nbsp;
Studios' shorter and smaller-scale scuffles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:07.620
but in terms of relevance to the plot and&nbsp;
visual style, it's a breath of fresh air.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:13.680
Shuri finally steps into a leadership role as&nbsp;
the Black Panther, literally standing as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:19.320
vanguard of her troops atop a massive military&nbsp;
vessel. They're planning to lure Namor to them so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:25.080
they can trap him in a retrofitted aircraft that&nbsp;
will dry him out and deplete his powers. Just as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:32.160
Namor is his people's god of the air, land, and&nbsp;
sea, this climactic conflict unfolds in the sky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:37.620
sand, and on the Atlantic. Riri Williams&nbsp;
gleefully buzzes through the clouds in her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:43.320
tricked-out Ironheart suit. Shuri crash-lands&nbsp;
on the shore, and the Black Panther and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:48.180
Feathered Serpent God slash at each other&nbsp;
acrobatically in the sand and flames. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:53.940
Dora Milaje use cables to take on the Talokanil&nbsp;
in an impressively choreographed vertical assault,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:58.860
while the Jabari defend the deck. It's&nbsp;
perfect for the story "Wakanda Forever"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:03.342
is trying to tell, which is about how war&nbsp;
is rarely in a nation's best interest.

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:10.440
This might sound like a backhanded compliment,&nbsp;
but the MCU's Namor looks way cooler than anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:15.120
who's familiar with the comics probably&nbsp;
expected. In his earliest illustrated form,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:20.640
Namor looks like a turn-of-the-century muscle&nbsp;
man in a belted speedo. And then there's the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:25.320
matter of those pointy elf ears and those&nbsp;
little angelic wings that grow out of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:31.260
feet. Even after Namor got an emo makeover&nbsp;
in the 2000s, writers and artists still had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:36.780
to contend with those quirks, as did Ryan&nbsp;
Coogler in "Wakanda Forever." As per usual,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:41.040
the writer-director was up to the task.&nbsp;
Namor is one of the highlights of the movie.

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:42.780
"My enemies call me Namor."

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:48.900
In part, that's thanks to the casting of Tenoch&nbsp;
Huerta and his performance, which ranges from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:53.400
endearing to frightening. And in part, that's&nbsp;
thanks to the character's new backstory and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:59.940
status as an indigenous Mexican god-king. Namor&nbsp;
still has his skimpy green shorts, but the costume&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:05.220
has been redesigned with native iconography&nbsp;
and materials. Somehow, even the image of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:11.580
mutant hovering in place — his tiny foot-wings&nbsp;
flapping fast — isn't ridiculous. All of this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:17.400
an enormous accomplishment, considering how often&nbsp;
Namor looks silly in comic books and how serious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:22.440
"Wakanda Forever" is for most of its runtime. The&nbsp;
only moments in which it's hard to take the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:28.080
and its anti-hero seriously come when the mutant&nbsp;
leaps and bounds through set pieces like Legolas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:34.800
doing parkour, or when he uses his winged feet to&nbsp;
dash across the sky, not unlike a hummingbird. CGI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:39.660
has come a long way, but it still can't make&nbsp;
superhuman feats like that look very natural.

